    stem: "AdBlue, a solution of urea (NH₂CONH₂) in water, is used in the exhaust systems of some diesel-powered vehicles to remove NO₂ from the hot exhaust flow by making use of the following reaction. 4NH₂CONH₂ + 6NO₂ → 7N₂ + 8H₂O + 4CO₂ catalyst 400 ⁰C",
