    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 OL Q10(c)(iv)",
    stem: "The NASA Perseverance Rover that landed on Mars in 2021 contained MOXIE, a small test unit designed to extract oxygen by electrolysis from the Martian atmosphere, which is mostly carbon dioxide, according to the following balanced equation. 2CO₂ → O₂ + 2CO In a test conducted in April 2021 on Mars, MOXIE produced 5.4 g of O₂ in one hour.",
