    stem: "The ancient Greeks argued that all matter was made up of just four ‘elements’: earth, air, fire and water. We now know that there are over 100 elements that are listed in the periodic table of the elements. Earth, air, fire and water are not included, as none of them is actually an element. Draw diagrams to show the arrangement of electrons in the main energy levels in (i) a neon atom, (ii) a fluorine atom.",
